WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:01.520
Okay.

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:07.980
A lot of people loved it when to close out
2019 I played a game of chess against producer

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:08.980
Pat.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.070
Check that out on YouTube.

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:12.469
We've got a video of it on our YouTube channel.

00:00:12.469 --> 00:00:16.070
It turns out that there are many chess players
in our audience.

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.320
I've played against some of them during live
streams that I've done.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:24.540
So today I am announcing we are having our
own chess tournament on Lee chess.org that's

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.890
the platform that we're going to be using.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:27.920
This is open to anybody.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.940
It doesn't matter how good you are, doesn't
matter how bad you are.

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:36.329
It's open to absolutely everybody who wants
to play the tournament will take place.

00:00:36.329 --> 00:00:43.860
Not this Tuesday, next Tuesday, February 21st
at 8:00 PM Eastern time, assuming no crazy

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:47.360
things happen because of, you know, Trump
impeachment causing debates to be moved or

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.290
whatever the plan is.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:54.460
Tuesday evening, February 21st 8:00 PM this
will be a one hour tournament.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:56.899
Some tournaments go on for hours and hours
and hours.

00:00:56.899 --> 00:00:59.950
We're a political talk show, so I think a
one hour chess tournament is appropriate.

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:05.889
We will be playing a format that is what's
called three plus two meaning each player

00:01:05.889 --> 00:01:08.210
will start with three minutes.

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:13.049
Every move you make, you get an incremental
two additional seconds for each move that

00:01:13.049 --> 00:01:14.400
you make.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.289
I will be live streaming my participation
in it, so if you don't want to play, you can

00:01:18.289 --> 00:01:19.689
just watch me participate in it.

00:01:19.689 --> 00:01:22.090
I am certainly not going to win this tournament.

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:27.070
There is some really good chess players in
our audience and I expect, uh, I'm taking

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:30.939
the position that merely to compete is an
honor and that I have no expectations as to

00:01:30.939 --> 00:01:32.009
how I will do.

00:01:32.009 --> 00:01:37.740
Uh, so we will link to, we won't have the
link for the tournament until about half an

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.509
hour before it starts.

00:01:39.509 --> 00:01:40.569
I will tweet it out.

00:01:40.569 --> 00:01:44.380
We will have the link on our YouTube and Twitch
streams that will be going on.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:50.649
So join the fun Tuesday, February 21st 8:00
PM Eastern time winner will get something

00:01:50.649 --> 00:01:53.889
we were thinking of of of a nice custom made
trophy.

00:01:53.889 --> 00:01:56.159
You can get trophies made, custom engraved.

00:01:56.159 --> 00:01:57.159
It's not that expensive.

00:01:57.159 --> 00:01:58.170
We can send it out to the winter.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:01:59.170
That's one idea.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:03.149
Uh, I dunno, I'm open to ideas for what the
winners should get, but I hope you will participate.

00:02:03.149 --> 00:02:05.950
My goal, we've never done anything like this
before.

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:07.840
My goal is to have 50 participants.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.440
I don't know if that's high or low.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:13.170
I know that there are at least a couple dozen
chess players in our audience, whether they

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:16.670
will all be available at 8:00 PM on Tuesday,
the 21st to participate in this.

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:17.670
I don't know.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.090
Um, but I hope you'll join us.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:21.360
It's going to be great.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:22.590
The winner will get something.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:23.670
It'll go for an hour.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:33.200
I would suggest that if you want to play plan
to get online about 15 minutes early@sevenfortyfiveandmakeanaccountonleechess.org

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.930
in advance.

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:39.480
That's ally chess.org totally free website
to, to play on.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:41.980
I'm David Pakman on that website.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:46.620
The reason I say get on 15 minutes before
is make sure that you have time to get the

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.380
link for the tournament.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:51.560
Make sure you hit join tournament and then
it's just good to wait.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:54.010
There'll be a countdown to the start of the
tournament.

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:55.010
That's my suggestion.

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:58.820
I will have more information about this upcoming,
but very exciting stuff.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:01.360
50 players is my goal and hopefully we will,
uh, we will achieve that.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:01.530
Okay.

